      "time_updated": 1789863826318
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the embedding strategy**\n\nOkay, I've decided to move forward with OpenAI's `text-embedding-ada-002` model for the embedding functionality within `embed_for_search.py`. I'll explicitly incorporate OpenAI's API usage into the code to handle the embedding process. I'm focusing on making the provider and model easily identifiable for future modification or extension.\n\n\n**Implementing the embedding function**\n\nI'm now implementing the embedding function within `embed_for_search.py` using the OpenAI SDK. The goal is straightforward: embed queries and documents. I've chosen `text-embedding-ada-002` and will ensure the provider (OpenAI) is clearly designated for easy switching later. I will add the code directly to the file to handle the embedding.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863828925,
          "start": 1789863826319
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc32938f001T6QhPWlPrtzvGz",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc328eaa001AJv5RBsML6IXwB",
      "session_id": "ses_f43cd7164ffe7muYZrohdFsYqQ",
      "time_created": 1789863826319,
      "time_updated": 1789863828925
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "loUyXYZ7e8rLmAwS",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nfrom openai import OpenAI\n\ndef embed_for_search(query: str, documents: list[str]) -> tuple[list[float], list[list[float]]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Embeds a query and documents for semantic search using OpenAI's embedding model.\n\n    Args:\n        query: The search query string.\n        documents: A list of document strings to embed.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple containing:\n            - The embedding of the query as a list of floats.\n            - A list of embeddings for the documents, where each document embedding is a list of floats.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = OpenAI(api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"))\n    model = \"text-embedding-ada-002\"\n\n    # Embed the query\n    query_response = client.embeddings.create(input=[query], model=model)\n    query_embedding = query_response.data[0].embedding\n\n    # Embed the documents\n    document_responses = client.embeddings.create(input=documents, model=model)\n    document_embeddings = [data.embedding for data in document_responses.data]\n\n    return query_embedding, document_embeddings\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # Set your OpenAI API key as an environment variable OPENAI_API_KEY\n    # For example: export OPENAI_API_KEY='sk-your-key'\n\n    search_query = \"What is the capital of France?\"\n    search_documents = [\n        \"Paris is the capital and most populous city of France.\",\n        \"The Eiffel Tower is a wrought-iron lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France.\",\n        \"Berlin is the capital of Germany.\",\n        \"The Louvre Museum is the world's most-visited museum and a historic monument in Paris, France.\",\n    ]\n\n    query_embed, doc_embeds = embed_for_search(search_query, search_documents)\n\n    print(\"Query Embedding (first 5 elements):\", query_embed[:5])\n    print(\"Number of Document Embeddings:\", len(doc_embeds))\n    print(\"First Document Embedding (first 5 elements):\", doc_embeds[0][:5])\n",
            "filePath": "embed_for_search.py"
          },
