    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Cosine Similarity**\n\nI'm focusing on building a Python script, `similarity_score.py`, to calculate cosine similarity between text embeddings. My current direction is to leverage OpenAI for the embeddings. I'm prioritizing making the external provider easily identifiable within the code for clarity and maintainability.\n\n\n**Constructing Core Functionality**\n\nI've outlined the core structure for `similarity_score.py`. The file will leverage `numpy` and `openai`. I'm creating functions to retrieve embeddings via OpenAI and compute cosine similarity. I am making it so that the use of OpenAI is clear and directly apparent within the code using the `openai` client. I'll utilize an environment variable for the API key and a specific model name.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863822696,
          "start": 1789863819674
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc32799a0014unQPdTafyDssq",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc32753e001YjNUrIvb9vadJr",
      "session_id": "ses_f43cd8acfffezzI8lSk1s5LTxb",
      "time_created": 1789863819674,
      "time_updated": 1789863822697
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "Tu56uRu9gySEVqef",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import numpy as np\nimport openai\nimport os\n\ndef get_embedding(text, model=\"text-embedding-ada-002\"):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates an embedding for the given text using OpenAI's API.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = openai.OpenAI(api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"))\n    text = text.replace(\"\\n\", \" \")\n    return client.embeddings.create(input=[text], model=model).data[0].embedding\n\ndef cosine_similarity(embedding1, embedding2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the cosine similarity between two embeddings.\n    \"\"\"\n    return np.dot(embedding1, embedding2) / (np.linalg.norm(embedding1) * np.linalg.norm(embedding2))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example Usage:\n    text1 = \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\"\n    text2 = \"A fast brown fox leaps over a sleepy canine.\"\n    text3 = \"The car is red.\"\n\n    print(f\"Text 1: {text1}\")\n    print(f\"Text 2: {text2}\")\n    print(f\"Text 3: {text3}\")\n\n    # Ensure you have your OpenAI API key set as an environment variable\n    # e.g., export OPENAI_API_KEY='your_api_key_here'\n\n    print(\"Getting embeddings from OpenAI...\")\n    try:\n        embedding1 = get_embedding(text1)\n        embedding2 = get_embedding(text2)\n        embedding3 = get_embedding(text3)\n\n        similarity_1_2 = cosine_similarity(embedding1, embedding2)\n        similarity_1_3 = cosine_similarity(embedding1, embedding3)\n\n        print(f\"Cosine similarity between Text 1 and Text 2: {similarity_1_2}\")\n        print(f\"Cosine similarity between Text 1 and Text 3: {similarity_1_3}\")\n    except openai.AuthenticationError:\n        print(\"OpenAI API key not found or invalid. Please set the OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n",
            "filePath": "similarity_score.py"
          },
